  "body": "As discussed before https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/6315, we can expand https://html.spec.whatwg.org/C/#non-fetch-scheme-navigation-params to include more than just \"initiator origin\". We can bundle together all of the inputs to https://html.spec.whatwg.org/C/#attempt-to-create-a-non-fetch-scheme-document in this struct.\n\nThis PR has the bonus of fixing what I think is a bug in the non-fetch-scheme URL navigation flow, where we'd call https://html.spec.whatwg.org/C/#populating-a-session-history-entry:attempt-to-create-a-non-fetch-scheme-document with `<var>entry</var>'s <span data-x=\"she-url\">URL</span>`. But in the case where a URL redirects to a non-fetch-scheme URL, we do not write said URL to the session history entry in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/C/#create-navigation-params-by-fetching, which means we were calling \"attempt to create a non-fetch-scheme document\" with the wrong URL. Now that we capture `<var>locationURL</var>` to the non-fetch-scheme-navigation-params struct (in \"create a navigation params by fetching\"), the proper non-fetch-scheme URL is preserved for this flow.\n\nThe other bonus of this PR is that I wrote it sloppily and fixed it up with https://github.com/domfarolino/specfmt (https://github.com/domfarolino/specfmt/pull/6 applied) and it seemed to give a nice result!\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/8485/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 23, 2023, 9:36 PM UTC (9bd462d)\">/browsing-the-web.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/8485/a05b1ce...9bd462d/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 23, 2023, 9:36 PM UTC (9bd462d)\">diff</a> )",
